Falsifies `kernel::virtio::tests::a_slot_whose_version_is_not_2_is_refused`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: the scan refuses only a slot whose `Version` reads 0, so a legacy slot (version 1) or
an undefined one is offered to a driver, and the kernel programs queue registers the legacy layout
does not have. This is what a release build did while the check was a `debug_assert_eq!`.

Expected to fail: the test's first `assert_eq!`, on version 1, which classifies as `Device`.

